{
  "$Comment": [
    "The sample shifting-floor arena for build_room.py: a hall over a pit whose middle floor drops away under a boss",
    "fight. The fight (the encounter script Zc_Encounter_Example, on the centre section, which never falls) signals",
    "Shift to the volumes carrying its arena tag, and the next section in the run's order cracks, falls and rises again",
    "(ShiftingFloor; two orders, so the run's seed picks one); every third Shift a rune pad on a side walkway glows, and",
    "a creature wearing the ward that comes onto it has the breakdown run on it (any effect and root interaction do for",
    "the sample). A Fire signal with a value turns a burst over one quarter of the hall at a time (ArenaQuadrants). A",
    "player who falls into the pit loses a share of their health, is told so and is put back on the south ledge; a",
    "creature wearing the boss's mark is set back on the centre section and any other dies (FallRescue). The arena tag",
    "is the script's own and plain, never @room. Cells are relative to the prefab anchor, the south doorway's floor",
    "cell; North is -Z."
  ],
  "Id": "Zc_Sample_Shifting_Floor",
  "Label": "Sample shifting floor",
  "Prefab": "ZiggfreedCommon.Samples.Zc_Sample_Shifting_Floor",
